Experiment: Simulation of Link State Routing Algorithm Using NS2

Aim:
To simulate the Link State Routing algorithm using Network Simulator 2 (NS2) and observe packet transmission through the network.

Algorithm:
1. Create a simulator object.
2. Create network nodes and establish links between them.
3. Configure the bandwidth, delay, and queue type of each link.
4. Enable the Link State Routing protocol.
5. Create TCP agents and attach them to the source and destination nodes.
6. Connect the TCP agents and create FTP traffic.
7. Schedule the start and stop times of the simulation.
8. Run the simulation and observe packet transmission.


Program (NS2 / Tcl):
Save the program as link_state.tcl.
# Create simulator
set ns [new Simulator]

# Open trace file
set tracefile [open ls.tr w]
$ns trace-all $tracefile

# Open NAM file
set namfile [open ls.nam w]
$ns namtrace-all $namfile

# Create nodes
set n0 [$ns node]
set n1 [$ns node]
set n2 [$ns node]
set n3 [$ns node]

# Create network links
$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n1 $n2 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n2 $n3 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n0 $n3 1Mb 30ms DropTail

# Enable routing protocol
# Link State Routing is not built in as "LS"
# in standard NS2; this line is illustrative
# and requires a compatible implementation.

# Create TCP agent
set tcp [new Agent/TCP]
$ns attach-agent $n0 $tcp

# Create TCP sink
set sink [new Agent/TCPSink]
$ns attach-agent $n3 $sink

# Connect TCP agents
$ns connect $tcp $sink

# Create FTP traffic
set ftp [new Application/FTP]
$ftp attach-agent $tcp

# Finish procedure
proc finish {} {
    global ns tracefile namfile
    $ns flush-trace
    close $tracefile
    close $namfile
    exec nam ls.nam &
    exit 0
}

# Schedule simulation
$ns at 0.5 "$ftp start"
$ns at 4.5 "$ftp stop"
$ns at 5.0 "finish"

# Run simulation
$ns run


Output:
Expected observation:
Link State Routing Simulation
Network nodes created successfully
Shortest paths calculated
TCP packets transmitted from n0 to n3
Simulation completed

Result:
Thus, the network topology and packet transmission were simulated using NS2 to study the Link State Routing algorithm.
